@title How a return request is decided
@subtitle Greenmoor Apparel customer care, current as of 2026-10-12

## Decision flow
diagram ret dir=TB title="Return decision flow"
ret: req "Return requested" user
ret: d30 "Within 30 days of delivery?" decision
ret: fs "Final-sale item?" decision
ret: decl "Decline return" svc
ret: lbl "Issue prepaid label" svc
ret: rec "Item received at warehouse" store
ret: insp "Inspection passes?" decision
ret: credit "Offer store credit at 50 percent" svc
ret: val "Order value over 200 dollars?" decision
ret: lead "Returns Lead review" team
ret: refund "Refund to original payment" svc
ret: req -> d30
ret: d30 -> decl : no
ret: d30 -> fs : yes
ret: fs -> decl : yes
ret: fs -> lbl : no
ret: lbl -> rec
ret: rec -> insp
ret: insp -> credit : no
ret: insp -> val : yes
ret: val -> lead : yes
ret: val -> refund : no
ret: lead -> refund : approved

## Service levels
table = step,target; Label issued,within 1 business hour of request; Inspection,within 2 business days of arrival; Refund posted,within 3 business days of inspection; Returns Lead review,within 1 business day

## Exceptions
- Damaged-on-arrival items skip the 30-day and final-sale checks.
- Gift returns always get store credit.
- Customers with more than 4 returns in 90 days are routed to the Returns Lead.
